+  How it draws
+  ------------
+  Textures and the target are surfaces in memory, described to OpenGPU as
+  slots. SDL's commands become one OpenGPU batch per RunCommandQueue:
+
+    clear, opaque fills           FILL
+    fills in any blend mode       FILL_BLEND
+    points, lines                 POINTS_BLEND, LINES_BLEND
+    copies                        COMPOSITE in SDL's blend mode, with alpha
+                                  (COPY when it is a plain 1:1 copy)
+    copies with colour            COMPOSITE_AFFINE: one command each,
+    modulation, rotation, flips,  nearest, linear or pixel art
+    the renderer's scale
+    SDL_RenderGeometry            TRIANGLES (SDL's form), clamped or
+                                  repeated on each axis
+    palette (INDEX8) textures     read through their PALETTE, so changing
+                                  the palette uploads nothing
+    YUV, NV12, NV21, P010         YUV into the texture's own ARGB32
+                                  surface, or YUV_SCALED straight into the
+                                  target when that is less work
+
+  Stream v1.7 (opengpu.library 0.19) carries what SDL 3 has beyond SDL 2:
+  the premultiplied blend modes, SDL_SCALEMODE_PIXELART, clamping one way,
+  palette textures, the RGBA32 and ABGR32 byte orders, P010, and the BT.709
+  full range and BT.2020 colour spaces. With an older library those draw on
+  the CPU, and their texture formats aren't offered, so SDL converts them.
+
+  OGPU_Query is asked for each operation on the target's format, so a back
+  end without an operation sends that command to SDL's own software code.
+  That code draws into the same surface after the batch so far has been sent
+  and finished. A frame is one submit: the copy of the window's surface to
+  the screen goes at the end of its last batch (SDL_os3gpu.h).
+
+  SDL chooses this renderer first when opengpu.library opens and the
+  window's surface is in a format OpenGPU draws; otherwise it chooses the
+  software renderer. SDL_RENDER_DRIVER=software picks the software one,
+  SDL_OPENGPU=0 keeps SDL off OpenGPU altogether, and SDL_OPENGPU_STATS=1
+  logs how many commands each path drew.
 */
